--TEST--
A child's uncaught throw arrives as data on the parent's result rather than as an exception unwinding into it: `ok` is false, `error` carries the class and the message as copied data, what the child echoed before throwing still crosses, and the parent runs on — ADR 0006 § *Failure is a value, not an exception*
--FILE nvs.toml--
# `rule:security/capability-check-at-the-door`: `spawn script` goes through a door that asks for
# `script.spawn` first, and deny-by-default means a case with no
# configuration cannot spawn at all. This grants it and nothing else.
[capabilities.script]
spawn = true
--FILE thrower.nvs--
<?nvs
// Written before the throw, so the parent's `output` carries it: the child's
// buffer is handed over at the join whichever way the child ended.
echo "child got this far";

throw new RuntimeError("the child could not finish");
--FILE returner.nvs--
<?nvs
// The other row of the same table: a top-level `return` is `ok = true`, and
// `error` is null rather than an error of some empty shape.
return "answered";
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:concurrency/a-child-s-failure-is-a-value
// ADR 0006 § *Failure is a value, not an exception*: there is no `try` around
// either call below and none is needed. Nothing unwinds across the boundary,
// for the reason nothing unwinds across a JIT frame (`rule:errors/propagation`) — the status
// is checked, so a child that fails cannot end the parent that spawned it.
var $bad = spawn script "thrower.nvs" with(output: "capture");
var $failed = await $bad;

echo "ok=", $failed->ok ? "true" : "false", "\n";

// "the class name and the message — as copied data, not the exception
// object". `error` is nullable because it is absent on the success row, so
// reading it costs a `?->` until the checker can narrow one off the `ok`
// test; `crates/nvs-types/src/expr/isolate.rs`'s module doc owns why the
// result is a shape and not a class.
echo "class=", $failed->error?->class, "\n";
echo "message=", $failed->error?->message, "\n";

// The throw did not cost the parent what the child had already written.
echo "output=", $failed->output, "\n";

// The success row, so the failure row is a bound asserted on both sides
// rather than a line read on its own.
var $good = spawn script "returner.nvs" with(output: "capture");
var $done = await $good;
echo "ok=", $done->ok ? "true" : "false", "\n";
echo "error=", $done->error == null ? "none" : "some", "\n";

// The line the whole section exists for.
echo "parent still running", "\n";
--EXPECT--
ok=false
class=RuntimeError
message=the child could not finish
output=child got this far
ok=true
error=none
parent still running
